---

# 9. Backend foundation

Create a clean FastAPI application.

The backend must have:

```text
FastAPI
Pydantic
SQLAlchemy
Alembic
PostgreSQL
```

Create a basic application entry point:

```text
backend/app/main.py
```

The application should start successfully.

---

# 10. API versioning

Use:

```text
/api/v1/
```

from the beginning.

Example:

```text
/api/v1/health
```

Do not create unversioned business APIs such as:

```text
/api/employee
```

Use:

```text
/api/v1/employees
```

in future phases.

---

# 11. Health API

Create a health endpoint:

```text
GET /api/v1/health
```

Expected response should indicate that the API is running.

For example:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "message": "API is healthy"
}
```

Keep the response format consistent and extensible.

---

# 12. Database foundation

Configure:

```text
PostgreSQL
SQLAlchemy
Alembic
```

Create the database connection layer.

Use environment variables.

Do NOT hard-code:

```text
database username
database password
database host
database port
```

---

# 13. Environment configuration

Create:

```text
.env.example
```

Include appropriate placeholders such as:

```text
APP_NAME=
APP_ENV=
APP_DEBUG=

DATABASE_URL=

REDIS_URL=

JWT_SECRET=

ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS=
```

Do not put real secrets in source control.

Create proper configuration management using Pydantic settings or an equivalent clean approach.

---

# 14. Database migrations

Configure Alembic correctly.

The project must support:

```bash
alembic upgrade head
```

and future migrations.

Do not manually modify database schema.

Every future schema change must be migration-based.

---

# 15. Redis foundation

Configure Redis.

The goal in Phase 1 is to establish the infrastructure.

Do not implement complex business background jobs yet.

Create a clean Redis configuration/service layer that can later support:

```text
Caching
Celery
Rate limiting
Sessions if required
Temporary data
```

---

# 16. Celery foundation

Configure Celery with Redis as the broker/backend where appropriate.

Create the basic worker structure.

Example:

```text
backend/app/workers/
```

Create a simple test task to verify that Celery can communicate with Redis.

Do not implement payroll/reporting jobs yet.

---

# 17. Frontend foundation

Create the React + TypeScript application.

Use:

```text
React
TypeScript
Vite
Tailwind CSS
```

The application should have a professional SaaS layout foundation.

Create:

```text
Sidebar
Top Header
Main Content Area
Responsive Layout
```

Do not implement full employee/attendance screens yet.

---

# 18. Frontend routing

Configure React Router.

Create basic routes:

```text
/
```

and an initial dashboard/home page.

Future routes should be easy to add:

```text
/dashboard
/employees
/attendance
/shifts
/leaves
/reports
/settings
```

Do not implement those business pages in Phase 1 unless required only as placeholders.

---

# 19. Initial dashboard

Create a clean foundation dashboard.

It can contain placeholder cards:

```text
Total Employees
Present Today
Absent Today
On Leave
```

IMPORTANT:

These values should be clearly identified as placeholder/demo values if the real backend modules do not yet exist.

Do not create fake business functionality.

The purpose is to verify the UI architecture.

---

# 20. Frontend API layer

Create a centralized API service.

Do NOT call APIs randomly from components.

Create something similar to:

```text
src/services/api/
```

or another clean architecture.

Future modules should be able to use:

```text
employeeApi
attendanceApi
leaveApi
reportApi
```

without duplicating HTTP configuration.

---

# 21. Error handling

Create a centralized backend error-handling mechanism.

Errors should:

* Return appropriate HTTP status codes.
* Return structured responses.
* Not expose stack traces to users.
* Log technical details securely.

Frontend should also have a reusable error handling mechanism.

---

# 22. Logging

Create structured logging.

Logs should eventually support:

```text
timestamp
log level
request ID
user ID
tenant ID
endpoint
execution time
```

Tenant/user fields may be unavailable in Phase 1, so design the logging system so they can be added later.

Never log:

```text
passwords
JWT tokens
refresh tokens
secrets
```

---

# 23. Request ID / correlation ID

Create middleware or infrastructure support for request IDs.

Example:

```text
Request
   ↓
Request ID
   ↓
API
   ↓
Database / Services
   ↓
Logs
```

This will make production debugging easier later.

---

# 24. CORS

Configure CORS through environment/configuration.

Do not use unrestricted production configuration such as:

```text
allow_origins=["*"]
```

as the permanent solution.

Development can be configured appropriately.

---

# 25. Docker

Create Docker support.

At minimum establish:

```text
backend
frontend
postgres
redis
```

Celery should also be runnable as a separate worker service.

Expected conceptual structure:

```text
Docker Compose
│
├── frontend
├── backend
├── postgres
├── redis
└── celery-worker
```

---

# 26. Docker networking

Ensure services can communicate using Docker service names.

Do not depend on hard-coded local machine IP addresses.

Example:

```text
backend → postgres
backend → redis
celery → redis
celery → postgres if required
frontend → backend
```

---

# 27. Development environment

Make local setup simple.

Document commands such as:

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

and:

```bash
docker compose down
```

Include database migration instructions.

---

# 28. Testing foundation

Create a pytest structure.

Example:

```text
backend/tests/
├── unit/
├── integration/
├── api/
└── conftest.py
```

At minimum create tests for:

```text
Health API
Application startup
Basic configuration
```

Do not create fake tests that only assert `True`.

Tests should verify actual behavior.

---

# 29. Frontend testing foundation

Set up the chosen frontend test framework.

Create at least one meaningful test for the initial application/dashboard rendering.

---

# 30. Code quality

Configure appropriate tooling.

Python:

```text
Ruff
Black
MyPy
Pytest
```

Frontend:

```text
ESLint
Prettier
TypeScript
```

Do not add tools merely for the sake of adding tools.

Use configuration that is practical for development.

---

# 31. Git

Create a proper `.gitignore`.

Ignore:

```text
.env
__pycache__
.pytest_cache
node_modules
dist
build
coverage
IDE files
Docker temporary files
logs
```

Never commit secrets.

