---

# 36. Security mindset

Treat security as a first-class requirement.

Do not:

* Hard-code secrets.
* Store passwords in plain text.
* Trust frontend authorization.
* Trust tenant IDs from the frontend.
* Expose stack traces.
* Log authentication secrets.
* Use unrestricted CORS permanently.
* Create insecure default credentials.

Security will become even more important in later phases.

---

# 37. Performance mindset

Design for scalability.

Avoid:

```text
N+1 database queries
Global mutable state
Unnecessary API calls
Blocking background work
Huge unpaginated responses
Duplicated business logic
```

Future APIs must support pagination and filtering.

---

# 38. IMPORTANT ARCHITECTURAL PRINCIPLE

Use separation of concerns.

For backend:

```text
Router
   ↓
Schema
   ↓
Service
   ↓
Repository
   ↓
Database
```

For frontend:

```text
Page
   ↓
Hook
   ↓
API Service
   ↓
Backend
```

Do not put all logic inside:

```text
main.py
```

or React page components.

---

# 39. QUALITY REQUIREMENT

Do not optimize for:

> "Make something that looks like it works."

Optimize for:

> "Build a foundation that can safely become a production SaaS product."

Code must be:

* Readable
* Maintainable
* Testable
* Modular
* Extensible
* Secure

---

# 40. PHASE 1 COMPLETION CRITERIA

Phase 1 is complete only when:

### Backend

* FastAPI starts successfully.
* `/api/v1/health` works.
* PostgreSQL connection works.
* SQLAlchemy is configured.
* Alembic is configured.
* Redis connection works.
* Celery worker can start.
* Configuration is environment-based.
* Logging works.
* Error handling works.
* CORS is configured.
* Request ID support exists.

### Frontend

* React starts successfully.
* TypeScript works.
* Tailwind works.
* Routing works.
* Basic SaaS layout works.
* API service layer exists.
* Basic dashboard renders.
* Responsive design works.

### Infrastructure

* Docker Compose works.
* PostgreSQL works inside Docker.
* Redis works inside Docker.
* Backend works inside Docker.
* Frontend works inside Docker.
* Celery worker can start.

### Testing

* Backend pytest configuration works.
* Health endpoint has a real test.
* Frontend has a meaningful initial test.
* All Phase 1 tests pass.

### Documentation

* README updated.
* Architecture documented.
* Development setup documented.
* Testing setup documented.

